## LeetCode 1480 — Running Sum of 1d Array

## Problem : 
Given an array, return the running sum of the array.
The running sum at index i is the sum of all elements from index 0 to i.
ex : input = [1, 2, 3, 4] , output = [1, 3, 6, 10]

## Approach :
- Initialize a variable runSum = 0 to keep track of the cumulative sum.
- Traverse the array using a for loop from index 0 to the end.
- Add the current element nums[i] to runSum.
- Store the updated runSum back into nums[i].
- Return the modified array after the loop

## Complexity :
Time Complexity = O(n) , traverse full Array
Space Complexity = O(1), no extra array created , modified the array itself with cumulative sum

SOLUTION : 
class Solution {

  // runningSum function 
    public int[] runningSum(int[] nums) {
        int runSum = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < nums.length; i++) {
            runSum += nums[i];
            nums[i] = runSum;
        }
        return nums;
    }

  // main function
    static void main(String args[]) {
      int[] nums = {1, 2, 3, 4};
      System.out.println(Arrays.toString(runningSum(nums[])));    
  }
}
